.TH FILE_OPEN 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
file_open \- open a file using Crunch modes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B long file_open(const char* path, int mode);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens path using FILE_READ, FILE_WRITE, or FILE_APPEND. Write and append
modes create files with permissions 0644 modified by the process umask.
Write truncates; append writes at the end.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a descriptor, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR open (3crunch),
.BR file_close (3crunch)
